 "evidence": "A two-year GCM test at 14 levels, one realization from the design climate's year-19 restart carried onto the levels by the conservative remap, set against the 10-level run with the same flags (A28R_301k_cold_sbm_rh07_deep200, without the shallow cap) and the rh 0.7 branch over the same years from the same restart: the first two years of a spin-up, so they show the direction and early size of the changes and not a settled climate. The 14-level run differs from deep200 in its levels and in the shallow cap together. The CM1 numbers are the settled boxes (the sea box's third lunar day, the land box's second), forced by Kuo's GCM. The off check compares the GCM's own output and restart bit for bit.",
 "reading_rule": "stages[stage][run]: rain by quarter (sunrise-noon, noon-sunset, sunset-midnight, midnight-sunrise; mm/day, all rain and the convective part) at the Near-side Sea's cells and the land box's cells; upper_air.at_heights_k the lunar-day mean at the sea cells taken onto the box's levels at equal shares of the surface pressure, at 18.9, 29.8, 41.8 and 55.8 km as box_upper_air does; <site>_lowest_level the sites' lowest level (sigma 0.9833 on both grids: temperature, vapour as a mixing ratio), the air at 2 m and the ground; global the yearly summaries' means with the area-mean rain, its convective share and the top two levels (sigma 0.038, 0.119; water in ppmv by volume); sea_t_minus_deep200_* the sea site's lunar-day mean temperature less deep200's, taken in ln sigma onto the other grid; the convective heating (W/m2 by layer, top first) and cloud cover by quarter at the sea site. off_check: every output variable and the restart of the 10-level year against deep200's year 0."
}
